Z||000007||88 Database Nut||04-21-2001||10:10 PM||||Yabba Dabba Do!  I have been outta town for three weeks WITHOUT internet service and am quite amazed and thrilled to find this thread!  Mega thanks for the info guys, It's going to help me reach that magic 11% mark soon!  Right now we're at around 1250 cars.  For anyone wondering about this project, it's basically like RAYDAR said, I'm trying to document the fates of each of the 26,402 '88s built.  The things I'd like are the vin of course, the factory colors (outside, inside and rims for the GTs), tranny option, it's fate/condition, and really anything you want to share about the car.  Owner name is NOT required, I'm tracking cars, not owners, but personal info is always welcome, and will be kept private if you desire.  Eventually (I keep saying it), i will have this online, and intend to make it possible for people to find out about the cars built next to theirs (to maybe bring people together who have sequential cars for a group pic or something).<P>Anyway, thanks for thinking of me guys, I'll add in what you've got here, keep em coming!<BR>John Willhoff, (770) 578-6556, also john.willhoff@lmco.com||||reg||1
